{
 "_source": "CAPRI GAMS source, gams/compile_rdp_data/build_general_set_structure.gms (the NUTS version correspondence CAPRI uses internally; 207 pairs, 184 distinct 8-character codes).",
 "_purpose": "Maps CAPRI's 8-character region codes to NUTS codes across coding-scheme versions. Needed because CAPRI's own result files use OLD numeric codes for member states that changed scheme - Italy writes IT110000 where NUTS-2016 says ITC1 - so validation lookups against CAPRI extracts silently matched zero Italian regions until this was found.",
 "_note": "A single CAPRI code can map to several NUTS codes across versions (IT110000 -> IT11 and ITC1). Consumers should prefer whichever candidate exists in the model's region set. | 2026-10: 75 CAPRI NUTS-2 codes added, each verified by CAPRI's total agricultural area matching the model region's base area (exact to 0.2%, or within 1% and unambiguous): France NUTS-2013->2016, Germany (NRW, RP, SL, ST, SH, TH), Bulgaria (CAPRI's own order: BG04->BG41, BG05->BG42, BG06->BG34), Greece, Italy, Poland, Sweden, Norway. Splits (one CAPRI region -> several model regions) stay with the national-remainder fallback. Each added pair also confirmed by a second variable (dairy cows, else wheat+barley area, within 3%); IT310000 (Trentino-Alto Adige = ITH1+ITH2, a split) had been matched to ITH4 by a coincidence of total area - corrected to IT330000->ITH4; unconfirmed pairs removed: [('NO090000', 'NO03'), ('PL500000', 'PL81')].",
